questionText:
Classic example: MediaPlayer interface has play(String filename). Your app already supports Mp3Player implements MediaPlayer. Now you need to support VLC and MP4 files via a third-party library that only exposes:

public class AdvancedMediaPlayer {
    public void playVlc(String filename) {
        System.out.println("Playing vlc file: " + filename);
    }
    public void playMp4(String filename) {
        System.out.println("Playing mp4 file: " + filename);
    }
}

You can't modify AdvancedMediaPlayer (it's a third-party jar). What's the correct Adapter structure here?

A weather app has its own TemperatureSensor interface expecting double getCelsius(). A legacy hardware SDK gives you LegacyFahrenheitSensor with only double getFahrenheit(), which you cannot modify. Which adapter correctly bridges this?

public class FahrenheitToCelsiusAdapter implements TemperatureSensor {
    private LegacyFahrenheitSensor sensor;

    public FahrenheitToCelsiusAdapter(LegacyFahrenheitSensor sensor) {
        this.sensor = sensor;
    }

    @Override
    public double getCelsius() {
        return (sensor.getFahrenheit() - 32) * 5.0 / 9.0;
    }
}

You're integrating a third-party payment SDK, StripeClient, which exposes charge(int amountInCents, String token). Your app's own code everywhere calls a PaymentGateway interface with void pay(double amountInDollars, String cardToken). Which is the correct adapter?

public class StripeAdapter implements PaymentGateway {
    private StripeClient stripeClient;

    public StripeAdapter(StripeClient stripeClient) {
        this.stripeClient = stripeClient;
    }

    @Override
    public void pay(double amountInDollars, String cardToken) {
        int cents = (int) Math.round(amountInDollars * 100);
        stripeClient.charge(cents, cardToken);
    }
}

A Duck interface has quack() and fly(). You have a Turkey class with gobble() and a weaker flyShortDistance(), and want to use turkeys wherever ducks are expected in a farm simulation. Which adapter correctly bridges this?

public class TurkeyAdapter implements Duck {
    private Turkey turkey;

    public TurkeyAdapter(Turkey turkey) {
        this.turkey = turkey;
    }

    @Override
    public void quack() {
        turkey.gobble();
    }

    @Override
    public void fly() {
        for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
            turkey.flyShortDistance();
        }
    }
}
